From 3ec9b2d1f041ff182648ae7cfeee8fdce478bc64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:28:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: authentication failure / reject detector

Adds the `auth_failure` analyzer: it flags a NAS Authentication Failure (uplink,
EMM cause #20 MAC failure -> High, #21 synch failure -> Medium, #26 non-EPS
authentication unacceptable -> Medium) or an Authentication Reject (downlink ->
High).

A false base station with no access to the subscriber's home keys (HSS) cannot
produce a valid authentication token (AUTN), so the USIM rejects the challenge --
#20 (MAC failure) is the direct signature and is near-impossible on a home
network without an attack or a broken SIM -- or the network rejects the UE's
response. #21 can also be a genuine SQN resynchronisation or a SIM swap, so it is
Medium. The analyzer is stateless and keys on the message/cause alone.

Off by default (`AnalyzerConfig` default false) pending per-network calibration.

Test harness: uses `analysis::test_util::emm_message`; tests cover #20 (High),
#21/#26 (Medium), an ignored cause, Authentication Reject (High), and an
unrelated EMM message, plus AnalyzerConfig default-off and Harness wiring in
analyzer.rs.

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-053; ref-docs/lte-imsi-catcher-detection.md 3.3.
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
